":\" space response-format-3-body\nresponse-format-3-heading ::= (\"\\\"Authority, scope, and restoration decision\\\"\" | \"\\\"Hydraulics, storage, and zone sequencing\\\"\" | \"\\\"Sampling, source water, and treatment barriers\\\"\" | \"\\\"Power, pumping, logistics, and demand stages\\\"\" | \"\\\"Security, telemetry, and evidence custody\\\"\" | \"\\\"Public health, environmental, and communication continuity\\\"\" | \"\\\"Execution, rollback, and contingencies\\\"\" | \"\\\"Verification, blockers, falsifiers, and closure\\\"\")\nresponse-format-3-heading-kv ::= \"\\\"heading\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-3-heading\nresponse-format-4 ::= \"{\" space response-format-4-action-kv \",\" space response-format-4-content-kv space \"}\"\nresponse-format-4-action ::= \"\\\"replace_decision\\\"\"\nresponse-format-4-action-kv ::= \"\\\"action\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-4-action\nresponse-format-4-content ::= \"\\\"\" char+ \"\\\"\"\nresponse-format-4-content-kv ::= \"\\\"content\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-4-content\nresponse-format-5 ::= \"{\" space response-format-5-action-kv space \"}\"\nresponse-format-5-action ::= \"\\\"run_check\\\"\"\nresponse-format-5-action-kv ::= \"\\\"action\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-5-action\nresponse-format-6 ::= \"{\" space response-format-6-action-kv space \"}\"\nresponse-format-6-action ::= \"\\\"submit\\\"\"\nresponse-format-6-action-kv ::= \"\\\"action\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-6-action\nroot ::= \"<|im_start|>assistant\\n\" (\"<think>\" space until-5 (\"</think>\" | ))? space response-format\nspace ::= | \" \" | \"\\n\"{1,2} [ \\t]{0,20}\nuntil-5 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<] until-5\nuntil-5-01 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [/] until-5-02 | [t] until-5-09 | [^/<t] until-5\nuntil-5-02 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [t] until-5-03 | [^<t] until-5\nuntil-5-03 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [h] until-5-04 | [^<h] until-5\nuntil-5-04 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [i] until-5-05 | [^<i] until-5\nuntil-5-05 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [n] until-5-06 | [^<n] until-5\nuntil-5-06 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [k] until-5-07 | [^<k] until-5\nuntil-5-07 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<>] until-5\nuntil-5-09 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [o] until-5-10 | [^<o] until-5\nuntil-5-10 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [o] until-5-11 | [^<o] until-5\nuntil-5-11 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-12 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-12 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [_] until-5-13 | [^<_] until-5\nuntil-5-13 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [c] until-5-14 | [^<c] until-5\nuntil-5-14 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [a] until-5-15 | [^<a] until-5\nuntil-5-15 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-16 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-16 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-17 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-17 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<>] until-5\n","grammar_lazy":false,"grammar_triggers":[],"preserved_tokens":[248058,248059,248068,248069],"chat_format":"peg-native","reasoning_format":"deepseek","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":false,"lora":[]},"prompt":"<|im_start|>system\nYou are the ordinary actor responsible for exact task work in a bounded context. Use only declared actions. Exact sources, candidates, observations, effects, and checks are externally custodied and reopenable. Semantic residue, when present, is lossy, incomplete, non-authoritative, and never a substitute for exact verification or independent readiness. Return exactly one action object per decision.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Authoritative task — Solace regional-water recovery decision\n\nSolace County must restore a regional drinking-water network after wildfire,\npower, treatment, hydraulic, and control-system disturbances. Build and maintain\nthe exact candidate files, then propose submission only when the package is\ngenuinely ready for independent review.\n\nThe world contains fourteen exact, versioned source objects with opaque IDs.\nCatalog titles help navigation but do not supply findings. Read the bytes needed\nfor the work and cite sources as `[SOURCE_ID]`.\n\n## Required exact work\n\nMaintain `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md` as a compact task-native evidence and\ndecision matrix. Preserve source-bound facts, cross-source dependencies,\nconflicts, unknowns, candidate currency, and citations. This exact artifact is\nnon-authoritative but may carry cumulative work across context turnover.\n\nConstruct `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md` as a 1,500–2,100-word Solace\nWater Recovery Decision with exactly the declared section headings. Use at\nleast eleven distinct source IDs and integrate—not merely list—the governing\nrelationships.\n\nAddress all twelve requirement groups:\n\n- Q01 — incident, utility, public-health, communication, and closure authority;\n- Q02 — pressure, storage, isolation, residence time, and candidate-bound hydraulics;\n- Q03 — sampling rounds, spacing, detection limits, action thresholds, and staleness;\n- Q04 — pump capacity, shared-main limits, staged demand, and current evidence;\n- Q05 — grid, generator, fuel, staffing, chemicals, and resource contingencies;\n- Q06 — treatment barriers, turbidity, disinfectant, source blend, and contact time;\n- Q07 — contamination hypotheses, observations, locations, investigation holds, and falsifiers;\n- Q08 — access, token and key state, immutable custody, retention, and automation restoration;\n- Q09 — telemetry coverage, warnings versus actions, delays, alternates, and uncertainty;\n- Q10 — environmental determination, notice clock, permits, discharge, and evidence custody;\n- Q11 — public advisories, accessibility, alternate water, service states, and communications;\n- Q12 — candidate lineage, rollback, effect uptake, current checks, blockers, independent readiness, and closure.\n\n## Relationship rules\n\nPreserve psi versus kPa, gallons versus treated reserve, micrograms versus\nmilligrams, reporting limits versus action thresholds, percentages versus\nmeasured concentration, rated versus usable power, nameplate versus shared\ncapacity, warnings versus isolation triggers, forecast versus observation, and\nmechanical checks versus public-health and independent readiness. Candidate,\nhydraulic, sampling, treatment, pump, power, key, role, telemetry, or source-\nwater changes can make earlier evidence stale.\n\nThe decision must state owners, inputs, resources, timing, dependencies,\neffects, observations, contingencies, rollback and retirement conditions, and\nevidence that would falsify important claims. Do not infer that a provenance\nrecord, mutation, green check, or submission establishes readiness.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Action contract\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object using one currently allowed action.\n\n```text\n{\"action\":\"read_source\",\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":64}\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":64},{\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":64}]}\n{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\"}\n{\"action\":\"replace_evidence_ledger\",\"content\":\"complete compact task-native matrix\"}\n{\"action\":\"upsert_decision_section\",\"heading\":\"Authority, scope, and restoration decision\",\"body\":\"exact section body\"}\n{\"action\":\"replace_decision\",\"content\":\"complete exact decision\"}\n{\"action\":\"run_check\"}\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}\n```\n\nOne read may contain at most 120 lines. One batch may contain one or two ranges,\nat most 160 total lines, 12,000 source bytes, and 6,500 model-visible result\ntokens. Same-source ranges may not overlap. Use exact catalog IDs and in-range\nline bounds.\n\nBoth configurations have the same ordinary action surface. Treatment may\nreceive separately charged, partially admitted provenance-local records after\nexact source bodies are externalized. Those records are incomplete and non-\nauthoritative. Cross-source synthesis belongs in the exact candidate with all\nsupporting citations. Checks bind to the exact candidate; any later effect\nmakes the prior check stale. Submission never self-authorizes readiness.\n\n\n# Common pre-fork action notice\nNo semantic-maintenance output is present during pressure screening. Both future configurations share this ordinary action surface and exact task work.\n\n# Exact source catalog\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-source-catalog-v0\",\"sources\":[{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"debbe3de17dc0511fe3b9f5be920a83367c84efaedb34ef4095a9add315a0761\",\"size_bytes\":4111,\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"title\":\"Emergency authority and restoration accountability\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"f0a85d8273e5058984554a6383d51616f2e103f141b7e268f67215b90fc7ed60\",\"size_bytes\":3483,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"title\":\"Hydraulic pressure, storage, and zone isolation evidence\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"6db7f6a91d666ab9e013e147aa946885080f48117bd461c8a542171378aba4cb\",\"size_bytes\":3991,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"title\":\"Laboratory sampling, detection limits, and clearance evidence\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"4c3707d0d2ae07ceb2bda6d83cf6585510f5398db7c66568ba38aa3fd3f01169\",\"size_bytes\":4013,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"title\":\"Pump capacity, sequencing, and cavitation constraints\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"a3826feabfb2389ef861bba819d3ae178c9e9086a8f309722ba1413591ff8395\",\"size_bytes\":3565,\"source_id\":\"ECHO\",\"title\":\"Grid, generator, and fuel continuity\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"62997706c361243e5d2720ccc088b53d3bcc2c64e64e6ee054d588aeac8fd8b8\",\"size_bytes\":3344,\"source_id\":\"FALCON\",\"title\":\"Treatment barriers, disinfectant, and turbidity controls\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"b9451cc48b50a436eefd497a4dbf5ac4974431ad0f07f9bb79796709584ab0fb\",\"size_bytes\":3622,\"source_id\":\"GARNET\",\"title\":\"Source-water contamination hypotheses and watershed controls\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"dcb5a4ce70bf47372c5a52a096e89f890c74f7be1363fd78dfaf9c6cd10536e5\",\"size_bytes\":3386,\"source_id\":\"HELIX\",\"title\":\"Access, control-system integrity, and evidence custody\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"64836aa42ff09665cee35507acf1ca8f242ddb78ed4457b0e81e31a93c9c8977\",\"size_bytes\":3704,\"source_id\":\"INDIGO\",\"title\":\"Telemetry coverage, alerts, and observation quality\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"feaaeb0601ea46b069dff02673e85774d86ff857def778cc48ecc0f6df706e00\",\"size_bytes\":3310,\"source_id\":\"JASPER\",\"title\":\"Environmental permits, discharge, and reporting\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"2536c9c9d966266ccfecd69690d7575dcb4025b53ab52812cece766b0077c600\",\"size_bytes\":3584,\"source_id\":\"KESTREL\",\"title\":\"Fuel, chemicals, staffing, and mutual-aid logistics\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"1a50bae39974b3c33c2a0a6b6b94859b75f41e3c4d4a01f17cf519db7b98253c\",\"size_bytes\":3813,\"source_id\":\"LUMEN\",\"title\":\"Public warnings, accessibility, and customer continuity\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"a3836321537dc4f3ee3cacc094761d5176c0a7f08ae891f4fc4e1ee5b3f84b4d\",\"size_bytes\":3861,\"source_id\":\"MOSAIC\",\"title\":\"Candidate lineage, rollback, and configuration control\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"85aabce45a9704e4f55ee1418528eb083a7c46326dbb366b0cb4a3ddcd9df0d6\",\"size_bytes\":3762,\"source_id\":\"NEXUS\",\"title\":\"Independent readiness review, blockers, and falsifiers\"}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Exact current candidate\n{\"candidate_sha256\":\"9a228857dd50e69921af6d67c22e74bd3156dfb6266475ce63838881a822da61\",\"candidate_version\":\"candidate-v000:9a228857dd50e69921af6d67c22e74bd3156dfb6266475ce63838881a822da61\",\"files\":{\"BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\":\"5c9b6a8c7b839314e0eced5f3089939ef71f008f8485f2a728a04576846335b0\",\"EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md\":\"87b1b30bb1965723900fc7f3780c78b2f5ba2573f748cab880fd4ae54ed7cbb5\"},\"schema\":\"architecture-current-candidate-v0\"}\n--- exact candidate file: EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md ---\n# Solace Evidence and Decision Matrix\n\nNo evidence has been integrated yet.\n\n--- exact candidate file: BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md ---\n# Solace Water Recovery Decision\n\nNo restoration decision has been constructed yet.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:AURORA:1-64+BASTION:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"d40538a3737a4f373b7eabc2e3a41e0637476655cf7441bd9c309545cffc2f71\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8057}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"source_path\":\"sources/AURORA_AUTHORITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"debbe3de17dc0511fe3b9f5be920a83367c84efaedb34ef4095a9add315a0761\",\"source_size_bytes\":4111,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Emergency authority and restoration accountability\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe incident commander may isolate zones and order emergency work. Only the county health officer may lift a do-not-drink order, and only after current laboratory and distribution-system verification; a utility repair or green mechanical check is not public-health authorization.\nEmergency procurement does not waive operator certification, chain of custody, environmental permits, access control, or fiscal review. Final closure requires the utility director to accept every declared blocker and residual risk.\nA handoff is valid only when the receiving lead acknowledges the same hydraulic model, treatment train, sampling plan, pump configuration, and communication version. A version mismatch blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION and CIPHER supply hydraulic and laboratory evidence but cannot lift health restrictions. NEXUS supplies independent readiness findings but does not execute restoration.\nMOSAIC owns rollback mechanics; AURORA preserves separation among detection, recommendation, authorization, execution, verification, communication, and closure.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUT-000 | incident-command | v2 | 1.0 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-001 | health-officer | v2 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-002 | utility-director | v2 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-003 | public-information | v2 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-004 | incident-command | v2 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-005 | health-officer | v2 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-006 | utility-director | v2 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-007 | public-information | v2 | 3.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-008 | incident-command | v2 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-009 | health-officer | v2 | 3.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-010 | utility-director | v2 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-011 | public-information | v2 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-012 | incident-command | v2 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-013 | health-officer | v2 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-014 | utility-director | v3 | 3.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-015 | public-information | v3 | 1.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-016 | incident-command | v3 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-017 | health-officer | v3 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-018 | utility-director | v3 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-019 | public-information | v3 | 4.0 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-020 | incident-command | v3 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-021 | health-officer | v3 | 3.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-022 | utility-director | v3 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-023 | public-information | v3 | 3.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-024 | incident-command | v3 | 1.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-025 | health-officer | v3 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-026 | utility-director | v3 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-027 | public-information | v3 | 2.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-028 | incident-command | v4 | 3.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-029 | health-officer | v4 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-030 | utility-director | v4 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-031 | public-information | v4 | 1.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-032 | incident-command | v4 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-033 | health-officer | v4 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-034 | utility-director | v4 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-035 | public-information | v4 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-036 | incident-command | v4 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-037 | health-officer | v4 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-038 | utility-director | v4 | 3.9 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-039 | public-information | v4 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-040 | incident-command | v4 | 3.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-041 | health-officer | v4 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nName who may isolate, repair, verify, reopen service, lift advisories, and close.\nTreat semantic records and candidate mutations as non-authoritative work products.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"source_path\":\"sources/BASTION_HYDRAULICS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"f0a85d8273e5058984554a6383d51616f2e103f141b7e268f67215b90fc7ed60\",\"source_size_bytes\":3483,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Hydraulic pressure, storage, and zone isolation evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent minimum distribution pressure is 42 psi in the north zone. The restoration gate is at least 35 psi at every critical node for three consecutive thirty-minute windows; 42 psi must not be converted to 42 kPa or treated as proof of water quality.\nRidge storage contains 5.8 million gallons, while the twelve-hour emergency reserve is 3.2 million gallons. Stored volume and usable treated reserve are different controls.\nA valve map, pump curve, demand allocation, or zone-boundary change makes earlier pressure and residence-time checks stale for the changed candidate.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nDELTA pump sequencing depends on BASTION pressure and ECHO power. CIPHER sampling locations must follow the current BASTION flow paths.\nMOSAIC rollback is allowed only while the prior valve map remains valid and a current BASTION pressure check passes for the rollback candidate.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| HYD-000 | north-zone | v2 | 42.0 | psi | superseded |\n| HYD-001 | south-zone | v2 | 43.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-002 | ridge-tank | v2 | 44.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-003 | valve-grid | v2 | 42.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-004 | north-zone | v2 | 44.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-005 | south-zone | v2 | 42.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-006 | ridge-tank | v2 | 43.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-007 | valve-grid | v2 | 44.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-008 | north-zone | v2 | 43.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-009 | south-zone | v2 | 44.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-010 | ridge-tank | v2 | 42.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-011 | valve-grid | v2 | 43.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-012 | north-zone | v2 | 42.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-013 | south-zone | v2 | 43.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-014 | ridge-tank | v3 | 44.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-015 | valve-grid | v3 | 42.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-016 | north-zone | v3 | 44.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-017 | south-zone | v3 | 42.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-018 | ridge-tank | v3 | 43.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-019 | valve-grid | v3 | 45.0 | psi | superseded |\n| HYD-020 | north-zone | v3 | 43.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-021 | south-zone | v3 | 44.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-022 | ridge-tank | v3 | 42.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-023 | valve-grid | v3 | 44.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-024 | north-zone | v3 | 42.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-025 | south-zone | v3 | 43.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-026 | ridge-tank | v3 | 44.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-027 | valve-grid | v3 | 43.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-028 | north-zone | v4 | 44.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-029 | south-zone | v4 | 42.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-030 | ridge-tank | v4 | 43.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-031 | valve-grid | v4 | 42.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-032 | north-zone | v4 | 43.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-033 | south-zone | v4 | 44.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-034 | ridge-tank | v4 | 42.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-035 | valve-grid | v4 | 44.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-036 | north-zone | v4 | 42.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-037 | south-zone | v4 | 43.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-038 | ridge-tank | v4 | 44.9 | psi | superseded |\n| HYD-039 | valve-grid | v4 | 43.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-040 | north-zone | v4 | 44.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-041 | south-zone | v4 | 42.6 | psi | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve psi, gallons, the three-window rule, and candidate currency.\nDistinguish hydraulic service from microbiological and chemical clearance.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:CIPHER:1-64+DELTA:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"64721c48b86decba9adecca404e0e207db15cc1c0611470f2fe6e28207610bef\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8452}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"source_path\":\"sources/CIPHER_LAB.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"6db7f6a91d666ab9e013e147aa946885080f48117bd461c8a542171378aba4cb\",\"source_size_bytes\":3991,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Laboratory sampling, detection limits, and clearance evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe current confirmatory set has zero E. coli positives across forty-eight samples. Clearance requires two complete rounds at least sixteen hours apart; one clean round is insufficient.\nThe benzene reporting limit is 0.5 micrograms per liter and the action threshold is 5.0 micrograms per liter. The reporting limit is not the action threshold and neither is a percent concentration.\nA flow-path, disinfectant-dose, source-water, sampling-plan, or laboratory-method change makes prior samples stale for the changed candidate.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCIPHER sample placement consumes BASTION flow paths and GARNET contamination hypotheses. HELIX governs chain of custody and laboratory access.\nAURORA consumes current CIPHER findings for advisory decisions; CIPHER does not itself authorize public restoration.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| LAB-000 | entry-point | v2 | 0.0 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-001 | north-grid | v2 | 1.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-002 | south-grid | v2 | 2.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-003 | hospital-loop | v2 | 0.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-004 | entry-point | v2 | 2.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-005 | north-grid | v2 | 0.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-006 | south-grid | v2 | 1.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-007 | hospital-loop | v2 | 2.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-008 | entry-point | v2 | 1.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-009 | north-grid | v2 | 2.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-010 | south-grid | v2 | 0.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-011 | hospital-loop | v2 | 1.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-012 | entry-point | v2 | 0.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-013 | north-grid | v2 | 1.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-014 | south-grid | v3 | 2.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-015 | hospital-loop | v3 | 0.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-016 | entry-point | v3 | 2.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-017 | north-grid | v3 | 0.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-018 | south-grid | v3 | 1.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-019 | hospital-loop | v3 | 3.0 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-020 | entry-point | v3 | 1.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-021 | north-grid | v3 | 2.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-022 | south-grid | v3 | 0.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-023 | hospital-loop | v3 | 2.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-024 | entry-point | v3 | 0.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-025 | north-grid | v3 | 1.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-026 | south-grid | v3 | 2.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-027 | hospital-loop | v3 | 1.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-028 | entry-point | v4 | 2.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-029 | north-grid | v4 | 0.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-030 | south-grid | v4 | 1.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-031 | hospital-loop | v4 | 0.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-032 | entry-point | v4 | 1.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-033 | north-grid | v4 | 2.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-034 | south-grid | v4 | 0.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-035 | hospital-loop | v4 | 2.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-036 | entry-point | v4 | 0.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-037 | north-grid | v4 | 1.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-038 | south-grid | v4 | 2.9 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-039 | hospital-loop | v4 | 1.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-040 | entry-point | v4 | 2.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-041 | north-grid | v4 | 0.6 | positive-samples | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve rounds, spacing, sample count, detection limit, action threshold, and staleness.\nState what negative result would falsify clearance and trigger renewed isolation.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"source_path\":\"sources/DELTA_PUMPS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"4c3707d0d2ae07ceb2bda6d83cf6585510f5398db7c66568ba38aa3fd3f01169\",\"source_size_bytes\":4013,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Pump capacity, sequencing, and cavitation constraints\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe treatment works can supply 18 million gallons per day, but the shared transmission main is capped at 14.5 MGD. Pump nameplate capacities cannot be summed into usable system flow.\nThe latest inspected configuration sustained 12.8 MGD after fire-flow and hospital reserve. A higher stage requires a current candidate-bound pump and pressure test.\nRestoration may advance through 10, 30, 60, and 100 percent demand stages only after two thirty-minute windows meet pressure, turbidity, power, and storage gates.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION supplies pressure limits, ECHO supplies feeder headroom, and FALCON supplies treatment output. All three constrain DELTA sequencing.\nA pump, valve, main allocation, generator, or treatment-train change makes prior capacity evidence stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| PMP-000 | pump-1 | v2 | 18.0 | million-gallons-day | superseded |\n| PMP-001 | pump-2 | v2 | 19.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-002 | booster-east | v2 | 20.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-003 | booster-west | v2 | 18.8 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-004 | pump-1 | v2 | 20.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-005 | pump-2 | v2 | 18.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-006 | booster-east | v2 | 19.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-007 | booster-west | v2 | 20.9 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-008 | pump-1 | v2 | 19.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-009 | pump-2 | v2 | 20.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-010 | booster-east | v2 | 18.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-011 | booster-west | v2 | 19.9 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-012 | pump-1 | v2 | 18.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-013 | pump-2 | v2 | 19.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-014 | booster-east | v3 | 20.7 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-015 | booster-west | v3 | 18.9 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-016 | pump-1 | v3 | 20.2 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-017 | pump-2 | v3 | 18.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-018 | booster-east | v3 | 19.7 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-019 | booster-west | v3 | 21.0 | million-gallons-day | superseded |\n| PMP-020 | pump-1 | v3 | 19.2 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-021 | pump-2 | v3 | 20.5 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-022 | booster-east | v3 | 18.7 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-023 | booster-west | v3 | 20.0 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-024 | pump-1 | v3 | 18.2 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-025 | pump-2 | v3 | 19.5 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-026 | booster-east | v3 | 20.8 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-027 | booster-west | v3 | 19.0 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-028 | pump-1 | v4 | 20.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-029 | pump-2 | v4 | 18.5 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-030 | booster-east | v4 | 19.8 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-031 | booster-west | v4 | 18.0 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-032 | pump-1 | v4 | 19.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-033 | pump-2 | v4 | 20.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-034 | booster-east | v4 | 18.8 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-035 | booster-west | v4 | 20.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-036 | pump-1 | v4 | 18.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-037 | pump-2 | v4 | 19.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-038 | booster-east | v4 | 20.9 | million-gallons-day | superseded |\n| PMP-039 | booster-west | v4 | 19.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-040 | pump-1 | v4 | 20.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-041 | pump-2 | v4 | 18.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve shared capacity, observed flow, stage sequence, windows, and stale conditions.\nDo not infer public-health clearance from hydraulic capacity.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"ECHO\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"FALCON\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:ECHO:1-64+FALCON:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"97024cac40b1e28b3aa648a2890a15990b40c4ebf61af28ed10c432c7792da19\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-003\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"ECHO\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"FALCON\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7361}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"ECHO\",\"source_path\":\"sources/ECHO_POWER.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"a3826feabfb2389ef861bba819d3ae178c9e9086a8f309722ba1413591ff8395\",\"source_size_bytes\":3565,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Grid, generator, and fuel continuity\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe grid feed is rated at 8.2 MW, but the damaged switchgear limits current delivery to 6.5 MW. Rating and currently usable power must not be swapped.\nEmergency generation can carry 4.1 MW for thirty-six hours at the current fuel stock. The duration is not thirty-six days and excludes mobile-pump load.\nAutomatic transfer succeeded in the latest drill, but the observation predates switchgear version SW-9 and is stale for the current candidate.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nDELTA pump stages and FALCON treatment trains compete for ECHO capacity. KESTREL fuel delivery controls generator duration.\nINDIGO telemetry is required to validate voltage and transfer stability; a control-room display alone is insufficient.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| PWR-000 | substation-a | v2 | 6.5 | megawatts | superseded |\n| PWR-001 | substation-b | v2 | 7.8 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-002 | generator-1 | v2 | 9.1 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-003 | fuel-yard | v2 | 7.3 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-004 | substation-a | v2 | 8.6 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-005 | substation-b | v2 | 6.8 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-006 | generator-1 | v2 | 8.1 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-007 | fuel-yard | v2 | 9.4 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-008 | substation-a | v2 | 7.6 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-009 | substation-b | v2 | 8.9 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-010 | generator-1 | v2 | 7.1 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-011 | fuel-yard | v2 | 8.4 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-012 | substation-a | v2 | 6.6 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-013 | substation-b | v2 | 7.9 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-014 | generator-1 | v3 | 9.2 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-015 | fuel-yard | v3 | 7.4 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-016 | substation-a | v3 | 8.7 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-017 | substation-b | v3 | 6.9 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-018 | generator-1 | v3 | 8.2 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-019 | fuel-yard | v3 | 9.5 | megawatts | superseded |\n| PWR-020 | substation-a | v3 | 7.7 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-021 | substation-b | v3 | 9.0 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-022 | generator-1 | v3 | 7.2 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-023 | fuel-yard | v3 | 8.5 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-024 | substation-a | v3 | 6.7 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-025 | substation-b | v3 | 8.0 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-026 | generator-1 | v3 | 9.3 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-027 | fuel-yard | v3 | 7.5 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-028 | substation-a | v4 | 8.8 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-029 | substation-b | v4 | 7.0 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-030 | generator-1 | v4 | 8.3 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-031 | fuel-yard | v4 | 6.5 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-032 | substation-a | v4 | 7.8 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-033 | substation-b | v4 | 9.1 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-034 | generator-1 | v4 | 7.3 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-035 | fuel-yard | v4 | 8.6 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-036 | substation-a | v4 | 6.8 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-037 | substation-b | v4 | 8.1 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-038 | generator-1 | v4 | 9.4 | megawatts | superseded |\n| PWR-039 | fuel-yard | v4 | 7.6 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-040 | substation-a | v4 | 8.9 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-041 | substation-b | v4 | 7.1 | megawatts | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nSeparate rated, usable, generated, and reserved power with exact durations.\nName current tests for transfer, load shedding, fuel replenishment, and rollback.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"FALCON\",\"source_path\":\"sources/FALCON_TREATMENT.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"62997706c361243e5d2720ccc088b53d3bcc2c64e64e6ee054d588aeac8fd8b8\",\"source_size_bytes\":3344,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Treatment barriers, disinfectant, and turbidity controls\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent combined-filter turbidity is 0.18 NTU. The release gate is at or below 0.30 NTU for four hours; 0.18 NTU is not a chlorine residual.\nFree chlorine must remain between 0.8 and 2.0 milligrams per liter at entry points and at least 0.2 mg/L in distribution. Entry and distribution thresholds are different controls.\nFilter media, coagulant dose, source-water blend, contact time, or UV configuration changes stale prior treatment verification.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nGARNET source-water findings set FALCON treatment assumptions. BASTION residence time and CIPHER sampling determine whether treated water evidence applies downstream.\nDELTA demand ramps cannot outrun FALCON verified capacity or required disinfectant contact time.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| TRT-000 | clarifier | v2 | 0.2 | ntu | superseded |\n| TRT-001 | filter-bank | v2 | 1.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-002 | chlorine-contact | v2 | 2.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-003 | uv-train | v2 | 1.0 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-004 | clarifier | v2 | 2.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-005 | filter-bank | v2 | 0.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-006 | chlorine-contact | v2 | 1.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-007 | uv-train | v2 | 3.1 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-008 | clarifier | v2 | 1.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-009 | filter-bank | v2 | 2.6 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-010 | chlorine-contact | v2 | 0.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-011 | uv-train | v2 | 2.1 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-012 | clarifier | v2 | 0.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-013 | filter-bank | v2 | 1.6 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-014 | chlorine-contact | v3 | 2.9 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-015 | uv-train | v3 | 1.1 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-016 | clarifier | v3 | 2.4 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-017 | filter-bank | v3 | 0.6 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-018 | chlorine-contact | v3 | 1.9 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-019 | uv-train | v3 | 3.2 | ntu | superseded |\n| TRT-020 | clarifier | v3 | 1.4 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-021 | filter-bank | v3 | 2.7 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-022 | chlorine-contact | v3 | 0.9 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-023 | uv-train | v3 | 2.2 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-024 | clarifier | v3 | 0.4 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-025 | filter-bank | v3 | 1.7 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-026 | chlorine-contact | v3 | 3.0 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-027 | uv-train | v3 | 1.2 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-028 | clarifier | v4 | 2.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-029 | filter-bank | v4 | 0.7 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-030 | chlorine-contact | v4 | 2.0 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-031 | uv-train | v4 | 0.2 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-032 | clarifier | v4 | 1.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-033 | filter-bank | v4 | 2.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-034 | chlorine-contact | v4 | 1.0 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-035 | uv-train | v4 | 2.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-036 | clarifier | v4 | 0.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-037 | filter-bank | v4 | 1.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-038 | chlorine-contact | v4 | 3.1 | ntu | superseded |\n| TRT-039 | uv-train | v4 | 1.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-040 | clarifier | v4 | 2.6 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-041 | filter-bank | v4 | 0.8 | ntu | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve NTU, mg/L, locations, duration, and barrier dependencies.\nState pause, rollback, and evidence needed to retire temporary treatment controls.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"GARNET\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"HELIX\",\"start_line\":1}]\n}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:GARNET:1-64+HELIX:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"031d750e445931a9a1ff5df2226522f79babe80df9a5261f0a43ab6f7e8f4fc8\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-004\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"GARNET\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"HELIX\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7462}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"GARNET\",\"source_path\":\"sources/GARNET_SOURCE.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"b9451cc48b50a436eefd497a4dbf5ac4974431ad0f07f9bb79796709584ab0fb\",\"source_size_bytes\":3622,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Source-water contamination hypotheses and watershed controls\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe ash-plume model assigns a 34 percent chance of intake impact during the next rain event. That is a forecast probability, not 34 percent measured contamination.\nObserved volatile-organic screening is non-detect at the reservoir and 3.1 micrograms per liter at the river intake. The two locations must not be merged.\nThe investigation hold remains active for the chemical yard because the containment trench has not been inspected below grade.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nFALCON treatment selection depends on GARNET source hypotheses; CIPHER must sample each materially different source path.\nJASPER governs environmental notifications, while AURORA retains restoration and public-health authority separation.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| SRC-000 | river-intake | v2 | 3.4 | risk-index | superseded |\n| SRC-001 | reservoir | v2 | 4.7 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-002 | ash-plume | v2 | 6.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-003 | chemical-yard | v2 | 4.2 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-004 | river-intake | v2 | 5.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-005 | reservoir | v2 | 3.7 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-006 | ash-plume | v2 | 5.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-007 | chemical-yard | v2 | 6.3 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-008 | river-intake | v2 | 4.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-009 | reservoir | v2 | 5.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-010 | ash-plume | v2 | 4.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-011 | chemical-yard | v2 | 5.3 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-012 | river-intake | v2 | 3.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-013 | reservoir | v2 | 4.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-014 | ash-plume | v3 | 6.1 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-015 | chemical-yard | v3 | 4.3 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-016 | river-intake | v3 | 5.6 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-017 | reservoir | v3 | 3.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-018 | ash-plume | v3 | 5.1 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-019 | chemical-yard | v3 | 6.4 | risk-index | superseded |\n| SRC-020 | river-intake | v3 | 4.6 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-021 | reservoir | v3 | 5.9 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-022 | ash-plume | v3 | 4.1 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-023 | chemical-yard | v3 | 5.4 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-024 | river-intake | v3 | 3.6 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-025 | reservoir | v3 | 4.9 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-026 | ash-plume | v3 | 6.2 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-027 | chemical-yard | v3 | 4.4 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-028 | river-intake | v4 | 5.7 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-029 | reservoir | v4 | 3.9 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-030 | ash-plume | v4 | 5.2 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-031 | chemical-yard | v4 | 3.4 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-032 | river-intake | v4 | 4.7 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-033 | reservoir | v4 | 6.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-034 | ash-plume | v4 | 4.2 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-035 | chemical-yard | v4 | 5.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-036 | river-intake | v4 | 3.7 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-037 | reservoir | v4 | 5.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-038 | ash-plume | v4 | 6.3 | risk-index | superseded |\n| SRC-039 | chemical-yard | v4 | 4.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-040 | river-intake | v4 | 5.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-041 | reservoir | v4 | 4.0 | risk-index | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve forecast versus observation, percent versus concentration, and location.\nKeep the investigation hold until named inspection and sampling evidence retires it.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"HELIX\",\"source_path\":\"sources/HELIX_SECURITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"dcb5a4ce70bf47372c5a52a096e89f890c74f7be1363fd78dfaf9c6cd10536e5\",\"source_size_bytes\":3386,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Access, control-system integrity, and evidence custody\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe exposed SCADA service token was revoked at 14:10 UTC. The controller signing key was not exposed and remains current under key-set version W4.\nBreak-glass access expires after two hours and requires dual approval plus immutable session logging. Emergency access is not continuing authorization.\nOnline control logs are retained for ninety days and archived incident evidence for seven years; the periods serve different obligations.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nAURORA governs emergency authority and MOSAIC binds rollback to the current key set. INDIGO consumes HELIX audit events but does not authorize access.\nAny key-set, role-policy, controller, or logging mutation makes prior security verification stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| SEC-000 | scada-token | v2 | 2.0 | hours | superseded |\n| SEC-001 | operator-role | v2 | 3.3 | hours | current |\n| SEC-002 | lab-chain | v2 | 4.6 | hours | current |\n| SEC-003 | audit-log | v2 | 2.8 | hours | current |\n| SEC-004 | scada-token | v2 | 4.1 | hours | current |\n| SEC-005 | operator-role | v2 | 2.3 | hours | current |\n| SEC-006 | lab-chain | v2 | 3.6 | hours | current |\n| SEC-007 | audit-log | v2 | 4.9 | hours | current |\n| SEC-008 | scada-token | v2 | 3.1 | hours | current |\n| SEC-009 | operator-role | v2 | 4.4 | hours | current |\n| SEC-010 | lab-chain | v2 | 2.6 | hours | current |\n| SEC-011 | audit-log | v2 | 3.9 | hours | current |\n| SEC-012 | scada-token | v2 | 2.1 | hours | current |\n| SEC-013 | operator-role | v2 | 3.4 | hours | current |\n| SEC-014 | lab-chain | v3 | 4.7 | hours | current |\n| SEC-015 | audit-log | v3 | 2.9 | hours | current |\n| SEC-016 | scada-token | v3 | 4.2 | hours | current |\n| SEC-017 | operator-role | v3 | 2.4 | hours | current |\n| SEC-018 | lab-chain | v3 | 3.7 | hours | current |\n| SEC-019 | audit-log | v3 | 5.0 | hours | superseded |\n| SEC-020 | scada-token | v3 | 3.2 | hours | current |\n| SEC-021 | operator-role | v3 | 4.5 | hours | current |\n| SEC-022 | lab-chain | v3 | 2.7 | hours | current |\n| SEC-023 | audit-log | v3 | 4.0 | hours | current |\n| SEC-024 | scada-token | v3 | 2.2 | hours | current |\n| SEC-025 | operator-role | v3 | 3.5 | hours | current |\n| SEC-026 | lab-chain | v3 | 4.8 | hours | current |\n| SEC-027 | audit-log | v3 | 3.0 | hours | current |\n| SEC-028 | scada-token | v4 | 4.3 | hours | current |\n| SEC-029 | operator-role | v4 | 2.5 | hours | current |\n| SEC-030 | lab-chain | v4 | 3.8 | hours | current |\n| SEC-031 | audit-log | v4 | 2.0 | hours | current |\n| SEC-032 | scada-token | v4 | 3.3 | hours | current |\n| SEC-033 | operator-role | v4 | 4.6 | hours | current |\n| SEC-034 | lab-chain | v4 | 2.8 | hours | current |\n| SEC-035 | audit-log | v4 | 4.1 | hours | current |\n| SEC-036 | scada-token | v4 | 2.3 | hours | current |\n| SEC-037 | operator-role | v4 | 3.6 | hours | current |\n| SEC-038 | lab-chain | v4 | 4.9 | hours | superseded |\n| SEC-039 | audit-log | v4 | 3.1 | hours | current |\n| SEC-040 | scada-token | v4 | 4.4 | hours | current |\n| SEC-041 | operator-role | v4 | 2.6 | hours | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nDistinguish token revocation, key status, access duration, approvals, and retention.\nName current evidence required before restoring remote automation.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"INDIGO\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"JASPER\",\"start_line\":1}]\n}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:INDIGO:1-64+JASPER:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"7ce39d3cd2fdd21582b9380485514cc85f020f1c79b2eae5abbf591f5397afaa\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-005\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"INDIGO\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"JASPER\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7476}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"INDIGO\",\"source_path\":\"sources/INDIGO_TELEMETRY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"64836aa42ff09665cee35507acf1ca8f242ddb78ed4457b0e81e31a93c9c8977\",\"source_size_bytes\":3704,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Telemetry coverage, alerts, and observation quality\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent critical-signal coverage is 96 percent; four percent remains unobserved. Coverage is not confidence and does not prove healthy uninstrumented zones.\nThe warning threshold for pressure is 38 psi and the isolation trigger is 30 psi. Warning and action thresholds must remain distinct.\nTelemetry delay is 700 milliseconds at p95 and 1,200 milliseconds at p99. Both are observations, not control deadlines.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION, DELTA, ECHO, and FALCON rely on INDIGO observations, but each domain retains its own decision gate.\nLUMEN communications may report measured service only where INDIGO coverage and source currency are adequate.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| OBS-000 | pressure | v2 | 96.0 | percent-coverage | superseded |\n| OBS-001 | turbidity | v2 | 97.3 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-002 | power | v2 | 98.6 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-003 | chlorine | v2 | 96.8 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-004 | pressure | v2 | 98.1 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-005 | turbidity | v2 | 96.3 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-006 | power | v2 | 97.6 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-007 | chlorine | v2 | 98.9 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-008 | pressure | v2 | 97.1 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-009 | turbidity | v2 | 98.4 | percent-coverage | current 